WEBVTT

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.360
What?

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.440
Bird's dead?

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.160
Yeah. The DNA matches Hachijou's.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.430
There's no doubt.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.170
From the look of things, it's suicide.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.790
What are you doing, Jirou?

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:22.090
I don't like idle chatter.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.040
Huh?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.790
Did you bring me out of my 
room to talk about this?

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.080
I'm going to shut the window.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.420
I'm borrowing this.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.750
Just like you'd said,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.450
Inagi Koutaro and Hachijou, AKA Bird, 
were working together behind the scenes.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.310
But Bird's death cost us another clue 
that we could have used against Inagi.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.390
<b>Booting</b>

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.270
<b>Biometrics Error</b>

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.270
I see. And?

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.090
You're quite calm.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.820
You should be more surprised.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.200
Bird is dead.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:49.900
Listen...

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:50.910
What?

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:55.240
Inagi may think he used Bird 
to get where he is now,

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.320
but he's the one who's been used.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.200
What are you trying to say?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.150
I told you, I don't like idle chatter.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.790
Bird is alive.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:06.800
Huh?

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.940
Without doubt.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.750
DNA is meaningless if 
the original data is wrong.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.120
He made himself appear to be dead

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.350
because that way, he could relax

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.110
and enjoy the game.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.800
<i>The space elevator will allow free 
travel between Earth and space.</i>

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.670
<i>The connecting device</i>

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:30.110
<i>that enables this dream by linking a 
sixth-generation carbon nanotube</i>

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.240
<i>will be revealed on the first day 
of the Tokyo City Summit</i>

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.030
<i>in front of Prime Minister Miyake and 
dignitaries from around the world.</i>

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.410
<i>Governor Inagi, the head of the project,</i>

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.700
<i>has said this is a chance to remind</i>

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.660
<i>the world of Japan's scientific power.</i>

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.460
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.410
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:04.850
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:22.050
<b>File 11: Dreams of an Idol</b>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.510
<b>Former Governor Terao's Mansion</b>

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.890
You're the eighth person to come here.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.780
When you were governor, why did 
you drop out of the election?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.950
What's this about?

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.060
Inagi Koutaro entered the election

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.350
to carry on Representative Naganuma's wishes.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.530
The media coverage gave him an advantage.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.660
His policies were attractive, 
and his popularity was rising.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.370
But...

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.520
Are you here to talk about old times?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.750
Or is this your way of getting back 
at me for my treatment of Unit 8?

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.750
I want to know why you dropped 
out of the election.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.950
I heard that some pundits thought 
you were more likely to win.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.460
You're quite persistent.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.110
I'll tell you what I think.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.680
During the Fisherman incident,

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.030
a data file detailing your 
corruption was leaked.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.870
But it was a trap to draw you out

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:12.640
that even involved our boss.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.690
You fell for the trap.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.580
You made a secret deal with Logos's 
Dog, AKA Doumoto Kakeru,

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.400
and Inagi gained blackmail material on you.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.110
Terao-san!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.190
I explained in the press conference, remember?

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.380
I dropped out for health reasons.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.230
But—

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.660
Your guess is wrong. Leave.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.350
I need proof!

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.370
Proof to defeat Governor Inagi!

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.140
Terao-san!

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.630
Phone call, sir.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.040
We're not done talking!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.390
As a former politician, 
there's one thing I can say.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.280
Representative Naganuma's suicide 
was a critical part of the plot

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.800
that was required for a nameless young 
man, Inagi, to get his big break.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.850
Is that...

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.030
Goodbye.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.920
Then Naganuma's death wasn't a suicide...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.150
Terao-san!

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:00.360
You can interpret that however you wish.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.610
This is the coroner who conducted 
the autopsy on Naganuma.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:08.780
<b>Name: Utsugi Tatsuhiko 
Age: 43 Years 
Birthplace: Tokyo City 
Job: Tokyo Medical Examiner's Hospital, 
Medical Examiner</b>

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.780
Utsugi Tatsuhiko, age 43.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.370
Send that to Kuroki-kun.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.240
Understood.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.200
How about something to drink?

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.330
Thank you.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.770
Something did feel wrong with

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.980
Representative Naganuma's death.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.120
But I couldn't pursue it.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:32.290
Maybe I unconsciously avoided it 
because I was afraid of the truth.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.330
Maybe if I had,

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.100
I could have stopped Inagi-kun earlier...

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.480
<b>Messages 
1 New Message 

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.480
Oh? It's rare for him to leave a message.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.840
Komieri-chan? It's me, Takeru.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.400
You remember that Diet member 
named Naganuma? Naganuma.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.050
If you know anything interesting 
about him, tell me at once!

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.020
Please.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:56.770
Bye!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.540
That's bad. Maybe he's figured it out...

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.420
Kominato-san! This was sent to the station!

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.080
If it's a fan letter, it can go 
with the rest at my office—

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.980
No, it says it's a medical report.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.120
I thought it might be important.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.600
<b>Medical Report</b>

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.250
A medical report?

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.600
Is it for a story?

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.290
I'll take a look. Thanks for bringing it to me.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.810
Oh, not at all.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.190
<b>Investigation Data Inside 

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.220
Utsugi?

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.550
Missing?

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.350
He hasn't answered the phone in a week,

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.910
and he hasn't gone to work at the hospital.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.970
Local police are looking for him.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.970
They already searched his home.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.540
Boss, you think he's behind this?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.110
Kuroki-kun, you're making assumptions.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.000
Boss!

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.830
I found Dr. Utsugi's communication records.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.080
Marimo-chan, the details, please.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.550
Sure, right away.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:53.510
<b>Call History</b>

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.780
In the few days before he disappeared,

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.570
he made multiple calls to the same person.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.510
Who?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.630
Um... I found it.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.640
Kominato Eriko?

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.770
The newscaster?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.440
Komieri-chan?

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.990
Kuroki always pulls this crap.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:09.860
We're not a childcare agency!

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.570
A childcare agency. That's clever.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.330
Oh, another one's coming?

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:17.260
Don't worry about me.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:20.830
I need an environment where I can 
drink coffee and have silence.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.300
And if you could lower the temperature...

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.600
Don't ask for too much.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.700
This isn't a coffee sh—

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.630
Hello!

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.690
Huh? The little sister?

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.090
Kuroki-san called and asked me 
to keep an eye on Jirou-kun.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.220
Keep an eye on him?

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.090
Yes.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.620
Here, I brought these, Jirou-kun!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.550
Hey, is that Komieri?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:50.240
Seriously?

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.020
Aren't you Kominato-san? The newscaster?

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.600
No. You have the wrong person.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.910
No, it really is you!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.290
I said I'm not!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.430
Don't worry, don't worry.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.370
We're fans of yours.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.080
Can we take a selfie? Please?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.780
Yay!

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.500
Yay.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.000
Yes!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Talk about lucky!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.960
Um, don't tell anyone I'm here—

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.230
Roger!

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:13.210
It's a secret between you and us!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.140
<b>Calling</b>

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.140
<i>...completed successfully, 
but there was no answer.</i>

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.100
It looks like she turned her phone off.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.350
Is she worried about being followed?

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.540
She hasn't been targeted by someone, 
like Dr. Utsugi was, right?

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.200
I hope not.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.630
<i>I found her!</i>

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.280
<i>Isn't this Komieri-chan?</i>

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.840
Facial recognition software picked her up.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.440
It seems to be someone's blog.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.330
Let me see.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:37.780
Sure.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:38.990
<i>Yay!</i>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.390
Um, what is this?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.830
<b>Finally got my photo with my beloved Komieri-chan!!!! 
But sadly... she's not as cute as she is on TV.</b>

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:42.680
I'm not sure.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:44.500
Jeez...

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.780
I know we need to be careful,

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:50.210
but why did it have to be such a creepy place?

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:54.930
Please don't let there be any 
cockroaches or rats...

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:58.760
That's it.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.480
<b>Kominato Eriko-sama</b>

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.590
A data card?

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.690
Yes!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.130
Hurry, hurry, hurry, hurry...

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:15.950
Got it!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.300
Utsugi-san?

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.840
Security camera footage of the morgue?

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:22.240
Representative Naganuma?

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.670
And someone else?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:24.720
Who's he talking to?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.340
<i>Suicide?</i>

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.030
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.630
<i>Naganuma-sensei committed suicide.</i>

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.760
<i>This is a clear case of murder.</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.760
I-Inagi Koutaro?!

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.800
<i>You want me to issue a false death certificate?</i>

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.070
No way...

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:43.630
How did he find this place?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:45.810
Kominato Eriko, yes?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.440
Those jackasses!

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.620
If a pheasant doesn't cry out, it won't get shot.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.290
My scoop!

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:03.970
It concerns Representative Naganuma!

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:04.450
Got it!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.380
Kuroki-san!

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.060
You saved me, Oscar VI.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.920
Well done, for you.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:27.920
Jeez...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:30.800
That's how you talk to the woman 
who saved your life?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.040
My scoop is in pieces...

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.850
Komieri-chan,

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.350
when you said it concerned Representative 
Naganuma, did you mean...

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.590
It was in the data Utsugi-san gave me.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.630
A conversation in the autopsy room 
with Inagi Koutaro.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.390
Inagi!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.470
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.470
It's been a while, everyone.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.080
That was good timing, Asami-chan!

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.430
Director General Kaidou

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:06.510
ordered Unit 9 to help guard the Tokyo Summit.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:10.610
And we saw that their command 
vehicle was passing by the scene,

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.160
so we made an emergency request.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.640
I see.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.980
Thank you, Asami-chan.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.320
I-It's nothing...

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.690
More importantly, boss,

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.170
what about my report?

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.580
Kominato-san, is this all right?

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.650
Yes, given the severity of the situation.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.540
I believe that when Governor Inagi

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:30.000
was a secretary, he used threats to 
obtain a fake death certificate.

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:33.000
Then Representative Naganuma's 
death really was...

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.840
Yes. Utsugi-san clearly calls 
it murder in the footage.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.680
In my interviews with him, 
he was less forthcoming.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.850
But he probably felt he was in danger, 
and decided to give me this footage.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.260
<b>Kominato Eriko-sama</b>

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:46.120
If we'd had it,

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:49.480
we could've finished him for sure!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.760
But with the data card in this shape...

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.540
Can it be repaired?

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.400
I'll try, but I doubt it...

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.220
What's wrong?

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.510
Dr. Utsugi was...

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:08.330
The local police say that Dr. Utsugi has 
been successfully apprehended...

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.210
Really?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:09.910
Yes.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:11.410
So he's safe...

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.720
How could he be in this state?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.590
<b>Tokyo Police Hospital</b>

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.590
He can't even say his own name.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.410
Doctors say his hippocampus 
was extremely swollen.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.180
His hippocampus?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.520
A memory transplant device?

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.790
He used that technology to silence Dr. Utsugi.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.490
Yes, this is Kuroki.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.600
Mythos wants to talk to you about something.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.320
Jirou does?

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.840
I heard what happened.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.010
I want you to check something.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:52.290
See if there's a Liko app installed on the 
mobile device with that footage.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:53.850
Why?

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:54.580
Just do it.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.660
The Liko app? Yeah, I used it.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.520
She says yes.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:01.090
What's with him?

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.000
I guess our last hope is gone...

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:10.200
<i>VIPs from all over the world are arriving</i>

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.900
<i>as the Tokyo City Summit is about to begin.</i>

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.480
<i>As they do, you'll see more police...</i>

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.480
You want us to call off the investigation?

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.940
I don't want to cause trouble during the summit.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:23.620
The government puts

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:27.470
a higher priority on the summit's success 
than the governor's arrest.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.890
Unit 8 will, as planned,

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:33.650
use its energy to guard the new city hall, 
where the summit's taking place.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.000
By the way, Chief Yamabuki...

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:36.800
Yes?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.100
About you and Governor Inagi...

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:41.000
There's no problem.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:45.330
If you're worried about my private 
relationship with the governor...

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.220
I see.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.640
Human history is about to 
undergo a great change.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:56.230
And it will start here in Tokyo.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.030
Boss, we've arrived at the platform.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.950
Everyone, I'm sure you have a lot to say,

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.530
but let's do something we 
can be proud of as police.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.170
Right!

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:15.160
Brain, Unit 8!

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.830
I'm here, Oscar VI.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.870
Thanks for coming.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:21.960
There's a lot more security than I expected.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.050
Well, media and VIPs from all 
over the world are here.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.060
They don't want to embarrass themselves.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.310
But I still didn't expect to see the USDF.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.020
They're going all-out.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.970
That's not Miho, is it?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.990
Oscar I, can you hear me?

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:38.850
Oscar I!

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.800
Good work out there today.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:57.040
I thought you'd be here soon.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.550
Inagi, you bastard...

00:14:58.550 --> 00:14:59.370
Kuroki-kun.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.560
You two will be responsible for guarding me.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.880
I want you to see my big moment up close.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.820
You—

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.140
Is it humiliating, Kuroki?

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:13.950
As long as you're a police officer, 
you have to obey the rules.

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.730
Once, I faced the same reality,

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:17.730
but I learned.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.060
You can't make dreams or reality come to pass

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.690
when you're bound by rules.

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:24.870
I'm counting on you.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:28.740
What's the satellite's status?

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:32.090
Counterweight and altitude are looking good.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.290
Okay, set the carbon nanotube.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.080
Setting carbon nanotube.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.310
Um, what are you doing?

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:41.950
Looking for a lost Liko.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.190
A lost Liko?

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.630
What does that mean?

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.950
You're aware that Liko is a cloud-based app.

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:48.510
And?

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:52.820
The original reason that Bird 
and I invented this app

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:57.090
was to use the system to collect 
data from every terminal.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:16:00.230
Um, what does that have to do with a lost Liko?

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:04.050
A Liko was on the mobile device 
that played the file.

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:08.610
Which means that Liko is wandering 
the network somewhere.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.150
But the amount of data is huge.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:14.710
Given a limited amount of time, 
I can't find it on my own.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:15.450
So...

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.450
So?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.820
<i>Transform!</i>

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:22.070
So I called Benu back.

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:24.380
<i>Yo! Long time, no see-see-see-see...</i>

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:31.700
Today is a revolutionary day for Earth.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:34.010
A worldwide revolution will 
begin here in Tokyo.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.940
The dream I've had since I 
became governor is about

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.520
to become reality before your eyes.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.250
Thank you, everyone.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:47.730
Look at this.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:51.440
For the first time, Earth and 
space will be connected

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.520
by a single carbon nanotube.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:58.350
It's still only a thin thread, 
the width of a human hair.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:01.260
But someday, it will be the space elevator

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:03.120
that humanity has dreamed of.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.590
Governor, the final preparations for 
the carbon nanotube are complete.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.670
Go ahead.

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:10.210
Yes, sir.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:12.140
Set carbon nanotube.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:12.670
Set.

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.550
Science is a wonderful thing.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:21.270
But its progress is a double-edged sword.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.780
And the increase in crime using illegal Willwears

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.030
is a problem requiring our immediate attention.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:30.570
As you saw from when the Logos 
Incident shut down the capital,

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.940
Japan's ability to manage the risk is low.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:35.030
We have been too defenseless.

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:38.700
My intent is to empower city, not national, 
government to handle threats,

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:45.410
and to create a civilian Willwear unit 
that reports directly to Tokyo City.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.070
Wonderful, Inagi-sensei.

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.940
Everything will be as you desire.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.300
<b>Data on All Parties, Electoral Areas, and Voting Blocs 
in Preparation for the Next Election 
of the Diet Lower House 

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:59.040
<i>Boing, boing, boing...</i>

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.740
They haven't found it yet?

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.530
They're using the command vehicle's systems, 
but there's too much information...

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:03.410
The wait is over, everyone.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.390
The carbon nanotube will soon descend.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:08.130
Look up at the ceiling.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:16.650
We have decided that, building upon

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:18.700
what we have learned

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.580
from the Tokyo experiment's success,

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.770
the first real space elevator will be

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.040
built in the Principality of Carupanuba.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.040
Zero adjustment needed. Maintain status.

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:28.250
Roger. Maintaining status.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.230
Playtime is over for you,

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:31.880
Bird.

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:36.410
What?

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:37.810
Look at the monitor in the hall.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.800
Kuroki-kun?

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:40.930
<i>I'm back!</i>

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.420
<i>Here goes Liko!</i>

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.430
<i>And click!</i>

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.030
This can't be...

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.140
<i>Movie start!</i>

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.480
<i>Suicide?</i>

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.240
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.690
<i>Naganuma-sensei committed suicide.</i>

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.270
<i>This is a clear case of murder.</i>

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.590
<i>You want me to issue a false death certificate?</i>

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>It's not a big deal, is it?</i>

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:04.440
<i>Compared to your past multiple malpractices.</i>

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:06.870
<i>Is that a threat, Inagi-sama?</i>

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.580
<i>A threat? How rude.</i>

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:12.720
<i>A transfer has already been 
made to your bank account.</i>

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.220
Why is this footage playing?

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:15.710
<i>Not having to work for over 
a decade is enough.</i>

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.710
This was my scoop!

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.160
No! This footage is fake!

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:19.620
<i>Why would you... Did you kill Naganuma?</i>

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.830
Chinju, what are you doing?

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:20.970
Turn off the monitors!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.890
<i>Naganuma-san was always good to me.</i>

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:24.080
I'm sorry! I've been trying, but...

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:27.730
<i>So I'm letting him be good 
to me until the end.</i>

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.930
It's not working. It's refusing our access.

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:30.610
Everyone, listen to me.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:34.570
This footage was faked to ruin me!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.970
I'm innocent! Believe me!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.030
Young fool.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.240
Of all the times to fail...

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.720
Kuroki...

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.490
Inagi, your ambitions end here.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.130
Turn yourself in.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.470
Was it you?

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:59.090
Did you set this up?!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:04.460
Interference with a police officer 
and attempted assault.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.430
That's not like you.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.890
You're pretty panicked!

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:09.920
Shut up!

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:13.630
After all I've done for you, 
you screw me at the very end!

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.310
You'll pay for that!

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:14.770
Oh, yeah?

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.400
That was my way of saying thanks.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:27.280
Thanks?

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:28.130
Yeah.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:30.930
When I was on the wrong path as a kid,

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.200
you led me back to the straight and narrow.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.430
So this is my way of...

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.600
Thanking me, huh?

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:46.580
I'm sorry, boss.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.020
No, if you hadn't done it, 
I would've punched him.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.020
Inagi-kun, not getting rid of this footage

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.730
was your biggest mistake.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.380
No, Rin...

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:01.000
My biggest mistake was

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.460
letting you refuse my proposal.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.120
Boss...

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:11.290
Sorry for interrupting,

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:14.080
but you'll pay for messing with my fun.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:14.980
Hachijou!

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:16.380
You're alive?!

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:20.180
The plan was to play dead

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.300
so I could publicly execute you.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:26.080
But you were the one who 
set this up, right, Mythos?

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.270
Nice job!

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.100
Bird!

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:32.060
The governor made contact with me 
when I was part of Logos.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:34.480
It sounded fun, and he was worth using,

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.900
so I helped him without telling Mythos.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:40.860
But he was such a wimp, I was disappointed 
with the way he did things.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:44.060
Anyway, I'm taking over as governor.

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:45.610
He can't mean...

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.890
We've lost access to the system.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:55.610
What?

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:58.250
What can he do with satellite control?

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:02.640
T-Tokyo will be destroyed.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.960
My Tokyo...

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.470
Tokyo will be destroyed?

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:08.760
I tried to stop it...

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:10.330
But it didn't work.

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:11.930
Tokyo is doomed!

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:20.320
I'll destroy everything you all 
worked so hard to build.

00:22:20.680 --> 00:22:23.670
It's the greatest ecstasy imaginable, you know?

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:56.540
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:57.130
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:08.210
File 12: Wonderful Days

00:23:57.130 --> 00:23:58.540
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:00.050
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:01.090
Good.

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:03.010
We all said it with no problem.

00:24:03.010 --> 00:24:05.340
Let's keep at it and get through the next episode.

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:07.120
Okay, I'll do it!

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:07.910
Me, too!

00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:08.510
Same here.

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:10.210
File 12: Wonderful Days
